        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Sample answer: starting with $2$ gives $5,\\ 45,\\ 43,\\ 45,\\ 20,\\ 2$.",
          "worked": "Starting with $2$:\n$$\\begin{align*}2+3&=5\\\\5\\times9&=45\\\\45-2&=43\\\\43+2&=45\\\\45-25&=20\\\\20\\div10&=2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q1-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Let the number be $x$ and apply the same operations. State your result. What is the final number?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x$.\n\nExpanding the brackets and collecting like terms shows that the procedure returns the starting number.",
          "worked": "The successive results are $x+3$, $9(x+3)$, $9(x+3)-2$, $9(x+3)-2+x$, $9(x+3)-2+x-25$, and $\\frac{9(x+3)-2+x-25}{10}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{9(x+3)-2+x-25}{10}&=\\frac{9x+27-2+x-25}{10}\\\\\\frac{9(x+3)-2+x-25}{10}&=\\frac{10x}{10}\\\\\\frac{9(x+3)-2+x-25}{10}&=x\\end{align*}$$\nThe final number is the number you started with.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 50
      }
